igner_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":"","claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Implemented the project configuration in the fresh `config-rich-text` worktree: added `[reconciler] rich_text_cutover = \"cloud\"` to `rebar.toml` and removed the adjacent stale statement that no reconciler keys remain. Verification: `rebar config` resolves `reconciler.rich_text_cutover = cloud [project]`; `git diff --check` passes; `rebar config validate` reports no removed inputs; `make lint` passes; focused config/rich-text tests pass (40 passed). Discovered bug `novel-unwasteful-stonefly` records that `rebar config validate` does not validate typed enum values.","timestamp":1787005456694729001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Gerrit change 1842: LLM-Review +1. Verified CI exposed one deterministic failure across Python 3.11/3.12/3.13: `test_canonical_outbound_equivalence.py::test_description_change_emits_description` expects the legacy plain-wire payload `{description: \"LOCAL\"}`, while the newly enabled Cloud codec correctly emits ADF-canonical Markdown `{description: \"LOCAL\\n\"}`. Local reproduction fails under project config and passes with `REBAR_RECONCILER_RICH_TEXT_CUTOVER=off`. Recommended remediation is to isolate this legacy golden-equivalence module from project operational config by explicitly setting the cutover off in its backend fixture, rather than changing production behavior or updating the golden to depend on the project setting. Awaiting operator approval because this expands the config-only ticket into a test-file change.","timestamp":1787006878546778001}],"created_at":1787004892545062001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"bde2a22d-6d86-4cb6-b258-7d45321fee71","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"3a76-ed19-0bfb-439d"},{"link_uuid":"d98039b1-4c30-4500-bcdd-7db4313a62ac","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"fa6f-e3e8-729f-45e2"}],"description":"## Context\nThe project Jira target is Jira Cloud (`https://navasage.atlassian.net`), while `reconciler.rich_text_cutover` defaults to `off`. Enable the already-shipped and tested Markdown↔ADF bridge behavior for this project without enabling the unrelated Data Center wire. This ticket is configuration enablement only; codec correctness remains covered by the existing rich-text unit and live-integration suites.\n\n## Plan\n- Add a `[reconciler]` table to the project `rebar.toml`.\n- Set `rich_text_cutover = \"cloud\"`.\n- Run `rebar config` from the worktree. This loads the typed config, rejects invalid enum values, and reports each resolved value with its precedence source.\n- Check the exact `reconciler.rich_text_cutover` output line and run `git diff --check`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `rebar.toml` contains `[reconciler]` with `rich_text_cutover = \"cloud\"`; verify by inspecting the focused git diff.\n- [ ] `rebar config` exits successfully, proving the typed loader accepts the value.\n- [ ] `rebar config` reports `reconciler.rich_text_cutover = cloud [project]`, proving both the resolved value and project-config provenance.\n- [ ] `git diff --check` reports no whitespace errors.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"rebar.toml","reason":"Enable the existing Jira Cloud rich-text cutover for this project."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","3a76-ed19-0bfb-439d"],["relates_to","fa6f-e3e8-729f-45e2"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"c0dfe433-1db5-41dd-b763-259af2773008","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["configuration","jira","rich-text"],"ticket_id":"52bf-bc40-3fcb-4729","ticket_type":"task","title":"Enable Jira Cloud rich-text reconciliation for rebar","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["6eaea2db-36b7-4668-afbc-49c0f50d32de","fb8c71b4-2b75-4c5f-aaaf-8dc30b3b7c18","444fbd8f-cef2-4864-a5c1-5b7d4ff0e4cb","f3bdb6ec-4dfc-499e-9ad0-4b29d58245d9","c0dfe433-1db5-41dd-b763-259af2773008","7314c6b9-9975-40ff-aede-79f84b1743eb","fbc1ef9d-c7a5-4eea-893b-656a6bd4ae85","bde2a22d-6d86-4cb6-b258-7d45321fee71","d98039b1-4c30-4500-bcdd-7db4313a62ac","e431adad-46f0-46ac-a107-df37b68e0ac2"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787011549257793261,"uuid":"5fb644f8-0fe0-44dc-8de3-b36aa760fbd8"}